{"card_hash": "106b34ae1c2190019181b7ded24e3ffa8017b76496262aca32faaf1cea954730", "channel": "IBM Technology", "chars": 10240, "chars_all_clips": 10240, "chars_chosen_clips": 1440, "clip_count": 15, "clips": [{"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=zYGDpG-pTho\u0026t=0s", "end": 63.32, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "0d765c1411c3ebcda9fd13f8ce76e99200ce8cccf2e045c7200193b7acd74fa5", "start": 0.94, "text": "Remember how back in the day people would Google themselves, you type your name into a search engine and you see what it knows about you? Well, the modern equivalent of that is to do the same thing with a chatbot. So when I ask a large lang", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=zYGDpG-pTho\u0026t=207s", "end": 254.869, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "b65ac23f00e91e73b40103b6c89b846f323926abc884bfc1825c66881cb4f061", "start": 207.38, "text": "So when you ask a query like, what was our company's revenue growth last quarter? Well, RAG will find documents that are mathematically similar in meaning to your question, even if they don't use the exact same words. So it might find docum", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=zYGDpG-pTho\u0026t=301s", "end": 351.43, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "c55538dc4e7cf08cfeb1608bb80af43f2a6aac3b199f45dec867c5a4ea40090d", "start": 301.48, "text": "So if we think about what we're having to do here, we've got documents that need to be vector embeddings, and we need to store these vector embedding in a database. All of this adds to processing costs, it adds to infrastructure costs to ma", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=zYGDpG-pTho\u0026t=451s", "end": 502.149, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "c61bef8f4031e2002a8845f836c5c3210d760a610da8f6a89a5276cbe6d634b0", "start": 451.15, "text": "So when we are putting the queries in, it's faster than RAG because it doesn't need to search through external data, and because the knowledge is kind of baked into the model's weights, you don't need to maintain a separate vector database,", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=zYGDpG-pTho\u0026t=502s", "end": 565.179, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "8a1261a20e60c9565142316d7a9754aa0eb2f8821dc4e3584841e941061929be", "start": 502.63, "text": "Updating a fine-tune model requires another round of training and then perhaps most importantly of all there is a risk of something called catastrophic forgetting. Now that's when the model loses some of its general capabilities while it's ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=zYGDpG-pTho\u0026t=704s", "end": 777.59, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "21e64047116d685b9edff38ff27b54185afe38325864d09a096c167e2082c3c8", "start": 704.99, "text": "And now, just now, we've talked about prompt engineering as well and I've really talked about those as three different distinct things here, but they're commonly used actually in combination. We might use all three together. So consider a l", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "AI and ML", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=zYGDpG-pTho\u0026t=0s", "end": 63.32, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "0d765c1411c3ebcda9fd13f8ce76e99200ce8cccf2e045c7200193b7acd74fa5", "start": 0.94, "text": "Remember how back in the day people would Google themselves, you type your name into a search engine and you see what it knows about you? Well, the modern equivalent of that is to do the same thing with a chatbot. So when I ask a large lang", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=zYGDpG-pTho\u0026t=207s", "end": 254.869, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "b65ac23f00e91e73b40103b6c89b846f323926abc884bfc1825c66881cb4f061", "start": 207.38, "text": "So when you ask a query like, what was our company's revenue growth last quarter? Well, RAG will find documents that are mathematically similar in meaning to your question, even if they don't use the exact same words. So it might find docum", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=zYGDpG-pTho\u0026t=301s", "end": 351.43, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "c55538dc4e7cf08cfeb1608bb80af43f2a6aac3b199f45dec867c5a4ea40090d", "start": 301.48, "text": "So if we think about what we're having to do here, we've got documents that need to be vector embeddings, and we need to store these vector embedding in a database. All of this adds to processing costs, it adds to infrastructure costs to ma", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=zYGDpG-pTho\u0026t=451s", "end": 502.149, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "c61bef8f4031e2002a8845f836c5c3210d760a610da8f6a89a5276cbe6d634b0", "start": 451.15, "text": "So when we are putting the queries in, it's faster than RAG because it doesn't need to search through external data, and because the knowledge is kind of baked into the model's weights, you don't need to maintain a separate vector database,", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=zYGDpG-pTho\u0026t=502s", "end": 565.179, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "8a1261a20e60c9565142316d7a9754aa0eb2f8821dc4e3584841e941061929be", "start": 502.63, "text": "Updating a fine-tune model requires another round of training and then perhaps most importantly of all there is a risk of something called catastrophic forgetting. Now that's when the model loses some of its general capabilities while it's ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=zYGDpG-pTho\u0026t=704s", "end": 777.59, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "21e64047116d685b9edff38ff27b54185afe38325864d09a096c167e2082c3c8", "start": 704.99, "text": "And now, just now, we've talked about prompt engineering as well and I've really talked about those as three different distinct things here, but they're commonly used actually in combination. We might use all three together. So consider a l", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "hint": null, "platform": "youtube", "profile": "librarian", "schema_version": 1, "selection_version": "spread-longest-v1", "slug": "RAG_vs_Fine-Tuning_vs_Prompt_Engineering_Optimizing_AI_Models", "source_revision": "9463b09f0d803f21be4b1e5400917d488490adc94a63b41ff1b1e38634eaf78f", "source_type": "video", "status": "evidenced", "summary_hint": null, "title": "RAG vs Fine-Tuning vs Prompt Engineering: Optimizing AI Models", "topic": "AI and ML", "truncated": true, "truncation": {"byte_budget": true, "fields": ["hint"], "selection": true}, "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zYGDpG-pTho", "video_id": "zYGDpG-pTho", "yoinked_at": "2026-05-12T18:32:23"}
